Checklist for adding a new TLP, i.e. a new committee with at least one project:

1. add the committee:
* create the committee RDF file in data/committees/ (copy _template.rdf and edit it)
* link to the RDF file in data/committees.xml
The script scripts/newtlp.py does both, from the committee-info.json entry:

    scripts/newtlp.py <pmc-id> [<pmc-id> ...]

It svn-adds the RDF file but does not commit. Check the diff it prints, then commit.
It cannot handle a committee coming back from the Attic.

2. add projects managed by the committee:
Project data comes from the ASF release catalog, which Apache Trusted Releases
builds from its own project records. ATR creates the committee itself from LDAP,
but not its projects: nothing here feeds them, so the PMC has to add them in ATR.
* a committee member uses Create project on the committee's page in ATR, or
* the project: block of the repository's .asf.yaml creates it on the next push.
Until then the committee is listed here with a stub entry built from
committees.json, and its page says the project is not yet in the catalog.

Project metadata is edited in ATR (https://releases.apache.org/projects/<key>?tab=metadata)
or in the project: metadata: block of .asf.yaml.

Data is not immediately reflected in https://projects.apache.org/: it will be processed daily at 2 AM UTC
